# nr-tui-core-gaps: what the lead applies (nothing here is applied by the task)

The six entries of mixdog-session-view/tests/fixtures/core-gaps.json, and what serves each:

  getSettingsSnapshot     -> config/getSettingsSnapshot     TuiClientService (new, tui_client_methods.rs)
  setProgressHint         -> thread/setProgressHint         TuiClientService
  restoreOlderTranscript  -> thread/restoreOlderTranscript  TuiClientService (answers false: the core keeps the whole log)
  restoreNewerTranscript  -> thread/restoreNewerTranscript  TuiClientService (same)
  rememberPromptHistory   -> thread/rememberPromptHistory   the thread actor (it owns the prompt writer): arm below
  inspectProjectPath      -> project/read                   already served (workspace service.rs, { path, exists, directory }); only the audit's table lacked the name

## native/core/crates/mixdog-core-session/src/session/mod.rs

After `pub mod turn_actions;` / `#[cfg(test)] mod turn_actions_tests;` add:

pub mod tui_client_methods;
#[cfg(test)]
mod tui_client_methods_tests;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-core-session/src/session/turn_ops.rs, fn is_actor_method

Add "thread/rememberPromptHistory" to the matches! list.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-core-session/src/session/actor/turn_ops.rs, fn turn_op

Beside the "thread/pushNotice" arm of `let done = match req.method.as_str()`:

            // rememberPromptHistory(text): the draft Esc cleared joins the cwd's persisted history, through the writer a submitted prompt uses
            // (the republish of the list is that writer's: PromptFlushed). true when there was a text to keep (Node answered whether the write
            // landed; the writer here retries a write that did not).
            "thread/rememberPromptHistory" => match super::super::tui_client_methods::remembered_prompt(&req.params) {
                Ok(Some(prompt)) => {
                    self.persist_prompt(prompt);
                    Ok(Value::Bool(true))
                }
                Ok(None) => Ok(Value::Bool(false)),
                Err(error) => Err(error),
            },

persist_prompt is private to the actor module and turn_ops.rs is its child (`use super::*`), so it is reachable there.

## the composition (mixdog-app-server-daemon, where TurnActionsService is registered)

Register one more domain service, the same way as TurnActionsService (it serves four exact methods; no op table). Its snapshot reads go
through the LateDomains of compose_domains.rs (`PreDomains.late`, the DomainCalls the setup status readers use, bound once the table is
built) and the web-search route through the WorkflowConfig (`PreDomains.workflow_config`):

    let web_route = pre.workflow_config.clone();
    let snapshot_reads = mixdog_core_session::session::tui_client_methods::SettingsReads::new(pre.late.clone(), move || web_route.web_search_route());
    builder.register(mixdog_core_session::session::tui_client_methods::TuiClientService::new(snapshot_reads, <the directory's Arc<dyn ThreadState>, the one ThreadProgressHints is given>));

(`pre` is whatever name the PreDomains has there. A read before LateDomains is bound fails and the snapshot shows null in its place; the
settings picker is not reachable before the core is up.)

Crate edges: none new (core-session already depends on mixdog-core-agents, -api, -ports, -base, -js, -tools, -store).

