inventory targets (getSettingsSnapshot, rememberPromptHistory, restoreNewerTranscript, restoreOlderTranscript, setProgressHint move from
Deleted("caller-less action") to their method), and the free-text rows. After applying: regenerate schema/*.json (client_methods.json
included) and the generated method-args files of packages/protocol-client (hot files).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-session-view/src/action_tables.rs, ARG_ORDER

The TUI calls setProgressHint(text, tone, percent); add the row (the test checks it is a permutation of the params' fields):

    ("thread/setProgressHint", &["text", "tone", "percent"]),

(getSettingsSnapshot({ heavy }) is one positional argument, the params' `options`; rememberPromptHistory(text) is one, `text`.)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-session-view/tests/fixtures/tui-store-calls.json

The member "inspectProjectPath" (class action) gets the target the sibling "renameProject" has:

   "target": {
    "method": "project/read"
   }

(after its "args" line, with a comma added on that line). With this, the five methods above in client_methods.json and the ARG_ORDER row,
`cargo test --offline -p mixdog-session-view --test protocol_coverage` sees no missing member, and core-gaps.json (emptied by this task)
is the proof.

